  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNODC Preventing and combatting corruption in Ukraine&apos;s recovery efforts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact: ANti-corruption authorities, policymakers, law enforcement officials and non-state actors collectively prevent and combat corruption effectively in Ukraine, thereby building resilience in Ukraine&apos;s recovery efforts in line with UNCAC 
Outcome 1: Integrity systems are strengthened in line with UNCAC
Outcome 2: Anti-corruption practitioners and other stakeholders apply their capacities to prevent and counter corruption
Outcome 3: Enhancing coordination, integration and oversight in Ukraine&#x2019;s recovery and reconstruction
Output 3.1 Coordination, integration and oversight

Main beneficiaries: State Agency for Restoration and Infrastructure Development (Reconstruction) of Ukraine (SARDI), National Anti-corruption Bureau of Ukraine (NABU), National Agency on Corruption Prevention (NACP), National Social Service Agency, and Ministry of Education.
Gender is mainstreamed in the project.</narrative>
  </description>
